  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The schematic image was not readable, so the wiring follows the sketch: pin 5 drives the white LED, and pins 2, 3 and 4 drive RGB red, blue and green. Each LED has a 220 ohm resistor on its anode side, and the common cathode and white LED cathode go to the ground rail.",
   "The ENV shield stacks on the MKR WiFi 1010 (joined edge). Its headers pass the board's pins through, so the jumper wires are attached to the MKR board's own pin ports D2 to D5 and GND. The shield's temperature sensor is on-board and needs no extra wiring.",
   "The catalogue lookup for the MKR ENV Shield returned the wrong part (MKR Relay Proto Shield), so arduino-mkr-env-shield is a new type with simplified port names that I chose.",
   "The parts list gives one 220 ohm resistor with no quantity. I used four, one for the white LED and one per RGB channel, because every LED needs a series resistor.",
   "The breadboard columns, and the LED legs going directly into the ground rail, are my own layout. The tutorial only says which pin goes to which LED.",
   "The Alexa app, Arduino Cloud and Cloud Editor are software only and are not nodes."
  ]
